sentences.l:
Close by to them came Medon and the divine minstrel
from the halls of Odysseus, when sleep had let them go,
and they stood in the midst;

And an immortal god, now before Odysseus
appeared, encouraging him, and now the suitors stirring up
rushed through the hall;

who a great deed did, with evil wanton-follies,
wasting the possessions and dishonouring the wife
of a man most excellent;

And now indeed all of them they would have killed and made unreturning,
if not Athena, the daughter of aegis-bearing Zeus,
had cried out with her voice, and held back the people, all.
